3113
02:07:42.190 --> 02:07:43.480
And that's my strength, right?

3114
02:07:43.480 --> 02:07:44.570
Like why haven't I done this?

3115
02:07:44.570 --> 02:07:48.460
So I am kind of excited to see what that's gonna be like.

3116
02:07:48.460 --> 02:07:49.730
I think you're gonna love it.

3117
02:07:49.730 --> 02:07:51.240
I think you're really gonna enjoy it.

3118
02:07:51.240 --> 02:07:53.620
Now you'll see in the process

3119
02:07:53.620 --> 02:07:56.410
to getting a out there and doing a few test swims,

3120
02:07:56.410 --> 02:07:58.590
you know my coaching strategies

3121
02:07:58.590 --> 02:08:00.900
are always around simulations

3122
02:08:00.900 --> 02:08:04.580
and I think you'll enjoy those alone in lakes and so forth.

3123
02:08:04.580 --> 02:08:05.940
And just getting comfortable with

3124
02:08:05.940 --> 02:08:09.293
that all day swimming pace again and zoning out into that.

3125
02:08:10.280 --> 02:08:11.980
Yeah. We're not quite there yet.

3126
02:08:13.480 --> 02:08:14.710
We're not quite there.

3127
02:08:14.710 --> 02:08:17.460
I had swam with any regularity in a very long time.

3128
02:08:17.460 --> 02:08:20.410
So my reintroduction to doing anything structured

3129
02:08:20.410 --> 02:08:23.100
in the pool has been humbling to say the least.

3130
02:08:23.100 --> 02:08:25.710
And before we even dive a little bit more into that,

3131
02:08:25.710 --> 02:08:29.603
I think it's worth talking a little bit about

3132
02:08:29.603 --> 02:08:32.883
on the subject of kind of humility, I suppose.

3133
02:08:34.020 --> 02:08:35.850
What just transpired with respect

3134
02:08:35.850 --> 02:08:38.850
to Jesse Itzler doing Ultraman Arizona

3135
02:08:38.850 --> 02:08:41.000
on ostensibly very little training

3136
02:08:41.000 --> 02:08:43.370
and the guidance that you gave him

3137
02:08:43.370 --> 02:08:46.200
and what transpired on Instagram

3138
02:08:46.200 --> 02:08:50.310
that we all watched with glee seeing him complete

3139
02:08:50.310 --> 02:08:52.400
that very difficult race.

3140
02:08:52.400 --> 02:08:55.037
And then we had talked earlier about your,

3141
02:08:55.037 --> 02:08:57.960
and he credited you and thanked you profusely

3142
02:08:57.960 --> 02:08:59.480
for the guidance that you gave him.

3143
02:08:59.480 --> 02:09:01.330
And now you're on the receiving end of

3144
02:09:01.330 --> 02:09:05.010
a lot of inbound emails and text messages.

3145
02:09:05.010 --> 02:09:06.837
Like, and I can just imagine, it's like,

3146
02:09:06.837 --> 02:09:09.140
"Oh, Jesse did Ultraman, Arizona, no training.

3147
02:09:09.140 --> 02:09:11.070
How can I do Ultraman and no training?"

3148
02:09:11.070 --> 02:09:13.083
Or any endeavor on no training?

3149
02:09:13.965 --> 02:09:16.910
Exactly. Which kind of misses the point. Right?

3150
02:09:16.910 --> 02:09:17.743
Yeah, it does.

3151
02:09:17.743 --> 02:09:19.190
And, but that's the thing about him.

3152
02:09:19.190 --> 02:09:21.290
And when we had that discussion in Minnesota,

3153
02:09:21.290 --> 02:09:24.440
two weeks prior to him doing Ultraman

3154
02:09:24.440 --> 02:09:27.000
is that I know him well enough

3155
02:09:27.000 --> 02:09:29.700
that he has a consistent training background.

3156
02:09:29.700 --> 02:09:32.290
I know that he's been cycling some

3157
02:09:32.290 --> 02:09:34.970
that he's always a consistent runner.

3158
02:09:34.970 --> 02:09:37.780
And so he has a platform to launch from,

3159
02:09:37.780 --> 02:09:40.380
this isn't literally at a zero.

3160
02:09:40.380 --> 02:09:43.670
And he has a history in to do hard things,

3161
02:09:43.670 --> 02:09:45.560
especially from a mental standpoint.

3162
02:09:45.560 --> 02:09:47.860
So you put all those ingredients together.

3163
02:09:47.860 --> 02:09:51.232
I felt pretty good about saying yes.

3164
02:09:51.232 --> 02:09:53.709
(both laughing)

3165
02:09:53.709 --> 02:09:56.060
Which yeah, I can't imagine you would be so quick

3166
02:09:56.060 --> 02:09:57.720
to say with other people,

3167
02:09:57.720 --> 02:10:01.170
like he does have that background and the mental game,

3168
02:10:01.170 --> 02:10:02.570
you know, the mental fortitude,

3169
02:10:02.570 --> 02:10:04.410
which is kind of what he leads with.

3170
02:10:04.410 --> 02:10:09.410
Yeah. And we discussed this sort of never defer approach.

3171
02:10:09.610 --> 02:10:11.830
And quite honestly, you know,

3172
02:10:11.830 --> 02:10:13.860
it brought up bigger emotions

3173
02:10:13.860 --> 02:10:16.530
and bigger thoughts as we were talking about it

3174
02:10:16.530 --> 02:10:17.963
even post the event.

3175
02:10:18.930 --> 02:10:22.600
He's had a lot go on in the last week in his life,

3176
02:10:22.600 --> 02:10:25.193
but he also had the opportunity.

3177
02:10:26.050 --> 02:10:28.520
He lost his father quite honestly.

3178
02:10:28.520 --> 02:10:33.520
And so he had the opportunity by not deferring,

3179
02:10:33.810 --> 02:10:36.610
doing this event with his father watching

3180
02:10:36.610 --> 02:10:40.020
and still taking part in this visual activity

3181
02:10:40.020 --> 02:10:42.520
and seeing him suffer and work through this.

3182
02:10:42.520 --> 02:10:47.190
And he was so proud and like had he not done this?

3183
02:10:47.190 --> 02:10:52.190
Like it just the universe how bizarrely it aligned

3184
02:10:52.220 --> 02:10:53.180
in this respect.

3185
02:10:53.180 --> 02:10:55.240
I mean, I haven't even talked to him about this aspect,

3186
02:10:55.240 --> 02:10:59.630
but never defer, at least go through the filter process,

3187
02:10:59.630 --> 02:11:01.390
talk to the people around you

3188
02:11:01.390 --> 02:11:04.470
and take chances because you never know

3189
02:11:04.470 --> 02:11:06.630
what the adventure and the experience will bring.

3190
02:11:06.630 --> 02:11:10.470
And so it was a special event with him

3191
02:11:10.470 --> 02:11:12.600
and yeah, you know what we spoke every evening,

3192
02:11:12.600 --> 02:11:14.530
I texted him during the event

3193
02:11:14.530 --> 02:11:17.060
so that the crew could read him things and so on.

3194
02:11:17.060 --> 02:11:19.450
But we knew that with fueling

3195
02:11:19.450 --> 02:11:22.376
and hydration and the proper mindset,

3196
02:11:22.376 --> 02:11:27.376
there is a way, a narrow way to navigate through this.

3197
02:11:28.200 --> 02:11:29.033
And he did it.

3198
02:11:29.919 --> 02:11:32.370
Right. He had to really thread the needle.

3199
02:11:32.370 --> 02:11:35.010
I know that the swim was the scariest part for him,

3200
02:11:35.010 --> 02:11:36.890
and he caught a bit of a break with that

3201
02:11:36.890 --> 02:11:39.010
because the chop and the wind was so crazy

3202
02:11:39.010 --> 02:11:40.810
that they called the swim off.

3203
02:11:40.810 --> 02:11:43.431
When I think he was about a kilometer

3204
02:11:43.431 --> 02:11:44.264
or a kilometer and a half into it.

3205
02:11:44.264 --> 02:11:46.680
And he got a bit of a breather before getting on the bike.

3206
02:11:46.680 --> 02:11:49.030
So I think that, you know,

3207
02:11:49.030 --> 02:11:51.010
basically put him in a good position

3208
02:11:51.010 --> 02:11:52.560
to be able to complete this thing.

3209
02:11:52.560 --> 02:11:55.440
And he can always say that he is an Ultraman.

3210
02:11:55.440 --> 02:11:58.680
And had he wavered, like you've said,

3211
02:11:58.680 --> 02:12:02.240
or deferred, perhaps it never would've come around again.

3212
02:12:02.240 --> 02:12:04.900
Or it would've come around again in a way

3213
02:12:04.900 --> 02:12:07.270
where he would've been less suited

3214
02:12:07.270 --> 02:12:09.140
or prepared to be able to complete it.

3215
02:12:09.140 --> 02:12:10.647
Well, you and I have talked about this before,

3216
02:12:10.647 --> 02:12:12.810
and this is ties us back to your event.

3217
02:12:12.810 --> 02:12:15.540
It's more a question of our lives are not going

3218
02:12:15.540 --> 02:12:17.573
to get emptier anytime soon.

3219
02:12:18.463 --> 02:12:20.100
That's what I told Jesse.

3220
02:12:20.100 --> 02:12:22.040
I keep diluting myself about that though.

3221
02:12:22.040 --> 02:12:23.753
I keep thinking like, it's gonna calm down,

3222
02:12:23.753 --> 02:12:25.710
like to my grave, right?

3223
02:12:25.710 --> 02:12:27.390
No. And that's what I said to Jesse.

3224
02:12:27.390 --> 02:12:29.660
I was like, "Do you think in a year from now,

3225
02:12:29.660 --> 02:12:31.790
if you defer all of a sudden your schedule

3226
02:12:31.790 --> 02:12:33.480
is gonna be emptier?"

3227
02:12:33.480 --> 02:12:36.060
Like his schedule is filling up left and right.

3228
02:12:36.060 --> 02:12:37.270
With all the projects.

3229
02:12:37.270 --> 02:12:42.270
Exactly. So I said, "Let's just take it now while you can.

3230
02:12:42.560 --> 02:12:44.650
And you're healthy. You're not injured.

3231
02:12:44.650 --> 02:12:47.220
It's a key ingredient for something like this

3232
02:12:47.220 --> 02:12:48.810
and we'll find out."

3233
02:12:48.810 --> 02:12:51.400
And he lived a true adventure.

3234
02:12:51.400 --> 02:12:55.090
And that is where you don't know if this is a reality

3235
02:12:55.090 --> 02:12:56.020
or if you can finish

3236
02:12:56.020 --> 02:12:58.440
and you really have to dig into a place,

3237
02:12:58.440 --> 02:13:02.490
he knows what an endurance adventure is like already

3238
02:13:02.490 --> 02:13:04.920
when you're trained for it, he's done enough of those.

3239
02:13:04.920 --> 02:13:05.770
Well, guess what?

3240
02:13:06.640 --> 02:13:10.110
He got to do something very few of us ever get to do.

3241
02:13:10.110 --> 02:13:12.100
Do one untrained,

3242
02:13:12.100 --> 02:13:15.660
like showing up at a hundred mile run with no training

3243
02:13:15.660 --> 02:13:18.010
or something like that, like just imagine that.

3244
02:13:18.961 --> 02:13:23.350
So that was something I was extremely proud of his grits

3245
02:13:23.350 --> 02:13:27.350
and resolved with that he did not let any voice get

3246
02:13:27.350 --> 02:13:30.023
in the way of his finish.

3247
02:13:30.890 --> 02:13:34.350
Yeah, well speaking of voices getting in the way,

3248
02:13:34.350 --> 02:13:36.550
I've got lots of voices in my head

3249
02:13:36.550 --> 02:13:39.600
that are angling to get in my way

3250
02:13:39.600 --> 02:13:41.960
and often succeed in that regard,

3251
02:13:41.960 --> 02:13:44.651
but I am really encouraged

3252
02:13:44.651 --> 02:13:47.360
and excited about this preparation phase

3253
02:13:47.360 --> 02:13:48.610
that I'm in right now.

3254
02:13:48.610 --> 02:13:51.830
So we've been working together

3255
02:13:51.830 --> 02:13:54.960
with some degree of intentionality for only like,

3256
02:13:54.960 --> 02:13:58.153
I don't know, four, six weeks at this point I think.

3257
02:13:59.080 --> 02:14:00.640
And taking it very gradually,

3258
02:14:00.640 --> 02:14:02.670
but just the consistency in the pool.

3259
02:14:02.670 --> 02:14:04.620
Like it's already kicking in.

3260
02:14:04.620 --> 02:14:06.760
I have so much muscle memory from swimming

3261
02:14:06.760 --> 02:14:09.690
that I trust and know that with regularity,

3262
02:14:09.690 --> 02:14:13.610
it will come back even though I'm getting up there in years

3263
02:14:13.610 --> 02:14:15.250
and it's been good to be able to

3264
02:14:15.250 --> 02:14:17.210
just get in the pool every day,

3265
02:14:17.210 --> 02:14:21.624
see just the tiniest bit of incremental improvement.

3266
02:14:21.624 --> 02:14:25.150
And I feel myself doing what I always do,

3267
02:14:25.150 --> 02:14:28.340
which is why is this workout only 3,500?

3268
02:14:28.340 --> 02:14:29.870
Like I can go 5,000.

3269
02:14:29.870 --> 02:14:31.087
I was gonna comment on that.

3270
02:14:31.087 --> 02:14:33.710
I have enough time to stack another 1500 on top of this.

3271
02:14:33.710 --> 02:14:34.790
And I have to remember,

3272
02:14:34.790 --> 02:14:37.860
I remember this in our Ultraman ramps up

3273
02:14:37.860 --> 02:14:40.200
where I would start feeling really fit

3274
02:14:40.200 --> 02:14:44.710
and get anxious about wanting to up the volume prematurely.

3275
02:14:44.710 --> 02:14:46.460
And always remembering

3276
02:14:46.460 --> 02:14:51.460
that slow build is part of building that strong foundation,

3277
02:14:51.540 --> 02:14:54.310
because it will get hard and it will get harder

3278
02:14:54.310 --> 02:14:57.540
than you think it's gonna get in time,

3279
02:14:57.540 --> 02:14:59.190
but at the right time.

3280
02:14:59.190 --> 02:15:00.023
At the right time.

3281
02:15:00.023 --> 02:15:02.070
And again it's keeping you healthy

3282
02:15:02.070 --> 02:15:04.930
and injury free and motivated throughout.

3283
02:15:04.930 --> 02:15:08.290
And so many people will enter into a great event

3284
02:15:08.290 --> 02:15:10.200
or an adventure or an experience.

3285
02:15:10.200 --> 02:15:13.870
And the first, you know, 10, 14 days,

3286
02:15:13.870 --> 02:15:16.559
they're all, gung ho on the training.

3287
02:15:16.559 --> 02:15:18.357
And next thing you know, it's like,

3288
02:15:18.357 --> 02:15:20.070
"This is a lot more than my body can handle

3289
02:15:20.070 --> 02:15:23.390
and that my life schedule can handle quite honestly.

3290
02:15:23.390 --> 02:15:25.520
I jumped in a little bit too aggressively."

3291
02:15:25.520 --> 02:15:26.980
And so I was also noticing

3292
02:15:26.980 --> 02:15:28.120
that with you sort of trying

3293
02:15:28.120 --> 02:15:31.210
to cheat in a few 5,000 yard swims.

3294
02:15:31.210 --> 02:15:33.860
So I want to keep in mind,

3295
02:15:33.860 --> 02:15:37.480
we wanted to be sure that you know what we're doing and why.

3296
02:15:37.480 --> 02:15:40.090
And so we're first building your endurance

3297
02:15:40.090 --> 02:15:43.610
and your endurance is gonna be about doing the distance.

3298
02:15:43.610 --> 02:15:45.860
And then it's gonna be about stamina,

3299
02:15:45.860 --> 02:15:49.780
which is about doing the distance faster, right?

3300
02:15:49.780 --> 02:15:51.660
That's the difference between the two,

3301
02:15:51.660 --> 02:15:53.600
one is how long can you go?

3302
02:15:53.600 --> 02:15:57.060
And what the other one is, how long can you go fast?

3303
02:15:57.060 --> 02:15:59.430
or fast relative to what we're looking to do,

3304
02:15:59.430 --> 02:16:01.560
for the event that we're getting ready for.

3305
02:16:01.560 --> 02:16:03.550
And so your confidence in being able

3306
02:16:03.550 --> 02:16:08.330
to swim around 30,000 yards is what you're sort of thinking

3307
02:16:08.330 --> 02:16:12.470
is going to revolve around us gently building our weeks,

3308
02:16:12.470 --> 02:16:15.950
so that then we can put the windows of training together,

3309
02:16:15.950 --> 02:16:17.710
where you have some extra time

3310
02:16:17.710 --> 02:16:20.560
that we can do some serious volume

3311
02:16:20.560 --> 02:16:24.460
and you build that confidence in a healthy

3312
02:16:24.460 --> 02:16:25.830
and enjoyable way,

3313
02:16:25.830 --> 02:16:28.080
because if your shoulders start hurting

3314
02:16:28.080 --> 02:16:29.280
or you're just depleted,

3315
02:16:29.280 --> 02:16:31.480
that's not gonna do us any good in May,

3316
02:16:31.480 --> 02:16:33.100
if your event is in June.

3317
02:16:33.100 --> 02:16:34.450
We wanna avoid that,

3318
02:16:34.450 --> 02:16:36.280
we wanna peak at the right time

3319
02:16:36.280 --> 02:16:39.150
and also build the confidence along with it

3320
02:16:39.150 --> 02:16:42.507
so that you hit the event, knowing, "I can do this."

3321
02:16:44.240 --> 02:16:46.100
I'm certainly not gonna head into this

3322
02:16:46.100 --> 02:16:49.440
with the kind of lack of preparation

3323
02:16:49.440 --> 02:16:51.230
that Jesse approached Ultraman,

3324
02:16:51.230 --> 02:16:54.090
but here we are at the beginning of May.

3325
02:16:54.090 --> 02:16:56.530
And this thing is in June.

3326
02:16:56.530 --> 02:16:58.040
Like that's not that much time.

3327
02:16:58.040 --> 02:16:59.000
It is a little bit scary.

3328
02:16:59.000 --> 02:17:00.787
And I think that motivates me like,

3329
02:17:00.787 --> 02:17:03.300
"Hey man we gotta make some hay here

3330
02:17:03.300 --> 02:17:05.600
or this is gonna be a disaster."

3331
02:17:05.600 --> 02:17:06.760
Well, and that's why we're sort

3332
02:17:06.760 --> 02:17:09.450
of gonna break it down into weeks where,

3333
02:17:09.450 --> 02:17:11.510
well, let's say 12 weeks to go.

3334
02:17:11.510 --> 02:17:13.740
12, 13 weeks, no pressure,

3335
02:17:13.740 --> 02:17:17.270
but that we have, you know, a long workout,

3336
02:17:17.270 --> 02:17:20.110
a long aerobic workout that you feel comfortable

3337
02:17:20.110 --> 02:17:21.740
and just not paying attention to pace,

3338
02:17:21.740 --> 02:17:25.140
but just swim your all day pace and do some long sets.

3339
02:17:25.140 --> 02:17:27.430
We'll do something where we're gonna do a lot of intervals

3340
02:17:27.430 --> 02:17:29.812
and steady state work where you feel

3341
02:17:29.812 --> 02:17:30.680
you look good about once again,

3342
02:17:30.680 --> 02:17:32.340
the stamina that you're building.

3343
02:17:32.340 --> 02:17:34.817
So how fast you're holding the steady states,

3344
02:17:34.817 --> 02:17:35.790
not best effort,

3345
02:17:35.790 --> 02:17:38.210
but just this is faster than I usually would swim.

3346
02:17:38.210 --> 02:17:41.740
But now I'm doing eight 200s or six 300s

3347
02:17:41.740 --> 02:17:45.020
instead of just shorter or less volume.

3348
02:17:45.020 --> 02:17:46.490
And then we'll do some workout

3349
02:17:46.490 --> 02:17:48.510
with some speed and drills in it,

3350
02:17:48.510 --> 02:17:50.850
so that you get your power back

3351
02:17:50.850 --> 02:17:53.730
and integrate all that into your swimming economy

3352
02:17:53.730 --> 02:17:56.280
so that you get back into the pool

3353
02:17:56.280 --> 02:17:58.660
and those thousands or eight hundreds

3354
02:17:58.660 --> 02:18:03.200
of going at all day pace feel really comfortable, steady,

3355
02:18:03.200 --> 02:18:06.433
and you have good traction on your pull through.

3356
02:18:07.292 --> 02:18:10.920
Quick footnote. I said, May I meant April?

3357
02:18:10.920 --> 02:18:13.231
We're at the beginning of April,

3358
02:18:13.231 --> 02:18:15.720
but either way, not that much time, it's been fun,

3359
02:18:15.720 --> 02:18:18.260
kind of on Instagram showing like the, you know,

3360
02:18:18.260 --> 02:18:20.700
I write out the workout in a Sharpie

3361
02:18:20.700 --> 02:18:22.340
and then I share it on Instagram stories

3362
02:18:22.340 --> 02:18:24.550
because I think people who aren't immersed

3363
02:18:24.550 --> 02:18:25.740
in the world of swimming,

3364
02:18:25.740 --> 02:18:26.730
think you just go to the pool

3365
02:18:26.730 --> 02:18:29.130
and you swim back and forth until your time is up.

3366
02:18:29.130 --> 02:18:31.950
And that's very far from the truth.

3367
02:18:31.950 --> 02:18:34.320
Everything is broken up into sets.

3368
02:18:34.320 --> 02:18:37.070
Every set has an intention.

3369
02:18:37.070 --> 02:18:39.390
And I'm always trying to read between the lines

3370
02:18:39.390 --> 02:18:41.970
when I look at the sets that you come up for me and think,

3371
02:18:41.970 --> 02:18:43.100
what is the purpose of this?

3372
02:18:43.100 --> 02:18:45.950
Like, why is this set coming after this one?

3373
02:18:45.950 --> 02:18:47.847
Oftentimes it's sort of like,

3374
02:18:47.847 --> 02:18:51.190
"Oh I see he wants me to ramp up to some tempo

3375
02:18:51.190 --> 02:18:54.030
or do a little bit of hypoxic breath work

3376
02:18:54.030 --> 02:18:55.840
and then go right into an aerobic set

3377
02:18:55.840 --> 02:18:59.130
to see how my body responds and how long

3378
02:18:59.130 --> 02:19:02.220
or quickly I can return to that baseline."

3379
02:19:02.220 --> 02:19:06.650
So it's all about like different modalities for acclimating

3380
02:19:06.650 --> 02:19:10.230
to an endurance race and then mixing it up with obviously

3381
02:19:10.230 --> 02:19:13.240
all the kind of technique based stuff drills, kick,

3382
02:19:13.240 --> 02:19:15.210
making sure all your body parts

3383
02:19:15.210 --> 02:19:16.850
are being trained properly as well.

3384
02:19:16.850 --> 02:19:18.210
Yeah. I mean you gotta figure,

3385
02:19:18.210 --> 02:19:21.397
we can't go out and swim 22,000 yards each workout, right?

3386
02:19:21.397 --> 02:19:24.870
You'll get really gassed up, therefore...

3387
02:19:24.870 --> 02:19:25.703
I can do that once.

3388
02:19:25.703 --> 02:19:26.600
I couldn't do that at all right now.

3389
02:19:26.600 --> 02:19:27.670
So therefore,

3390
02:19:27.670 --> 02:19:31.360
how do we make a 4,000-yard workout affect

3391
02:19:31.360 --> 02:19:34.070
when you're getting ready for 20,000 yards?

3392
02:19:34.070 --> 02:19:39.070
And so creating fatigue pockets, intensity breath work,

3393
02:19:39.190 --> 02:19:40.023
things like that,

3394
02:19:40.023 --> 02:19:42.600
and then returning to your go all day pace,

3395
02:19:42.600 --> 02:19:44.766
will highlight to you

3396
02:19:44.766 --> 02:19:46.660
how you're progressing in your fitness.

3397
02:19:46.660 --> 02:19:49.860
Creating insertion points that are supposed to fatigue you

3398
02:19:49.860 --> 02:19:53.050
and now how does that feel swimming a 400,

3399
02:19:53.050 --> 02:19:55.910
a 300 or a steady set from that?

3400
02:19:55.910 --> 02:19:57.710
And that's where we're at right now.

3401
02:19:58.863 --> 02:20:01.864
One of the other pieces to this

3402
02:20:01.864 --> 02:20:05.860
that I kind of presented you with is the idea

3403
02:20:05.860 --> 02:20:08.780
of building in some cycling into this

3404
02:20:08.780 --> 02:20:12.027
for the sole purpose of expanding my aerobic

3405
02:20:12.950 --> 02:20:16.890
like zone two base because I can ride my bike longer

3406
02:20:16.890 --> 02:20:17.880
than I can swim in the pool.

3407
02:20:17.880 --> 02:20:20.820
Right now I can go out for four hours, five hours,

3408
02:20:20.820 --> 02:20:22.490
maintain an elevated heart rate

3409
02:20:22.490 --> 02:20:24.420
for an extended period of time

3410
02:20:24.420 --> 02:20:26.670
without risk of injuring myself,

3411
02:20:26.670 --> 02:20:28.550
unless I get hit by a car or something like that.

3412
02:20:28.550 --> 02:20:30.360
Like I'm not gonna throw my shoulder out

3413
02:20:30.360 --> 02:20:32.000
or anything like that.

3414
02:20:32.000 --> 02:20:34.320
How do you think about that?

3415
02:20:34.320 --> 02:20:37.240
Like how beneficial is that going to be?

3416
02:20:37.240 --> 02:20:38.830
Should I just be in the pool

3417
02:20:38.830 --> 02:20:41.360
and maximizing that because we have so little time

3418
02:20:41.360 --> 02:20:44.800
or do you think that I'm getting a value add from that?

3419
02:20:44.800 --> 02:20:47.150
There is a value add, especially mentally

3420
02:20:47.150 --> 02:20:48.080
with regards to,

3421
02:20:48.080 --> 02:20:51.373
I know I can do a 2, 3, 4 hour activity right now,

3422
02:20:52.210 --> 02:20:53.760
where my heart rate is elevated.

3423
02:20:53.760 --> 02:20:56.010
And so that is definitely part of it.

3424
02:20:56.010 --> 02:20:58.630
I do that a lot with swimming and running as well.

3425
02:20:58.630 --> 02:21:01.770
I can go out, when I do a coast drive for example,

3426
02:21:01.770 --> 02:21:04.163
and I ride my bike six to eight hours a day.

3427
02:21:04.163 --> 02:21:06.330
Well that doesn't necessarily translate

3428
02:21:06.330 --> 02:21:08.200
into my running ability,

3429
02:21:08.200 --> 02:21:09.670
but it does translate to me

3430
02:21:09.670 --> 02:21:11.660
that I know I can do something continuously

3431
02:21:11.660 --> 02:21:13.000
for six to eight hours.

3432
02:21:13.000 --> 02:21:15.337
And so that helps build my confidence for running

3433
02:21:15.337 --> 02:21:16.600
and so forth.

3434
02:21:16.600 --> 02:21:18.920
And so that's how I would mainly approach it.

3435
02:21:18.920 --> 02:21:21.720
Yes, there is a fitness point in the beginning here

3436
02:21:21.720 --> 02:21:24.400
where your zone two and elevated heart rate,

3437
02:21:24.400 --> 02:21:28.760
just even in an aerobic space is going to be helpful,

3438
02:21:28.760 --> 02:21:30.840
delivering more oxygen into the working muscles

3439
02:21:30.840 --> 02:21:31.950
and so forth.

3440
02:21:31.950 --> 02:21:35.240
But eventually we're gonna hit a point where

3441
02:21:35.240 --> 02:21:37.260
that is truly active recovery

3442
02:21:37.260 --> 02:21:39.540
and mental space versus

3443
02:21:39.540 --> 02:21:42.440
the value of time in the pool, for sure,

3444
02:21:42.440 --> 02:21:44.429
but we're not there yet.

3445
02:21:44.429 --> 02:21:46.250
And I actually like that time out there

3446
02:21:46.250 --> 02:21:49.090
because you're using different muscles and the oxygen,

3447
02:21:49.090 --> 02:21:51.700
the stress is lower on the body.

3448
02:21:51.700 --> 02:21:54.150
So that then when you return to the pool,

3449
02:21:54.150 --> 02:21:57.173
there's a more intentional focus around it.

3450
02:21:58.040 --> 02:22:00.820
Right and it also gives my upper body muscles

3451
02:22:00.820 --> 02:22:03.390
a day to bounce back a little bit

3452
02:22:03.390 --> 02:22:05.300
so that when I am in the pool,

3453
02:22:05.300 --> 02:22:08.680
it's not just junk miles or what have you.

3454
02:22:08.680 --> 02:22:10.770
I can be a little bit more focused and fresh

3455
02:22:10.770 --> 02:22:12.470
and try to get the most out of it.

3456
02:22:13.550 --> 02:22:14.403
Yes. For sure.

3457
02:22:15.450 --> 02:22:17.280
One question about zone two.

3458
02:22:17.280 --> 02:22:18.570
So when I'm on the bike,

3459
02:22:18.570 --> 02:22:22.190
like I know what my zones are, heart rate wise,

3460
02:22:22.190 --> 02:22:24.400
assuming they haven't varied dramatically

3461
02:22:24.400 --> 02:22:28.230
from what they used to be, but when I'm in the pool,

3462
02:22:28.230 --> 02:22:29.830
I'm not wearing a heart rate monitor.

3463
02:22:29.830 --> 02:22:31.340
I'm not really paying attention to that.

3464
02:22:31.340 --> 02:22:35.040
I do have, I could be like a total tried dork

3465
02:22:35.040 --> 02:22:37.749
and wear that stuff in the pool.

3466
02:22:37.749 --> 02:22:39.120
Lots of people do that.

3467
02:22:39.120 --> 02:22:39.953
And stop your watch.

3468
02:22:39.953 --> 02:22:43.503
And you gotta stop your watch after every 150.

3469
02:22:44.853 --> 02:22:45.960
And click it when you do the drills

3470
02:22:46.860 --> 02:22:49.570
to make sure that it's logging your yardage accurately.

3471
02:22:49.570 --> 02:22:51.500
Yeah. For kicking.

3472
02:22:51.500 --> 02:22:52.333
Yeah, exactly.

3473
02:22:52.333 --> 02:22:55.390
Because I have such a, like yourself,

3474
02:22:55.390 --> 02:22:57.090
like such a robust background in swimming,

3475
02:22:57.090 --> 02:22:58.420
like I'm pretty connected.

3476
02:22:58.420 --> 02:23:01.690
I know what my kind of effort levels are to achieve that,

3477
02:23:01.690 --> 02:23:04.030
but if somebody's watching this or listening to it

3478
02:23:04.030 --> 02:23:05.870
and they're thinking about how

3479
02:23:05.870 --> 02:23:07.472
they're approaching their training in the pool,

3480
02:23:07.472 --> 02:23:12.203
how does the conversation around zones apply to that person?

3481
02:23:13.600 --> 02:23:16.940
That's where we often have an 800 or a 600

3482
02:23:16.940 --> 02:23:20.110
or a 500 at the end of a swim practice,

3483
02:23:20.110 --> 02:23:22.410
sort of where you jump into your all day pace.

3484
02:23:22.410 --> 02:23:24.960
We wouldn't do it as much by heart rate,

3485
02:23:24.960 --> 02:23:27.070
but we're not gonna be testing heart rate,

3486
02:23:27.070 --> 02:23:29.320
but at the end of a workout, let's say, you say, all right,

3487
02:23:29.320 --> 02:23:33.630
I'm just gonna no clock or get my time for 500,

3488
02:23:33.630 --> 02:23:36.360
but it's gotta feel like my go all day swim pace.

3489
02:23:36.360 --> 02:23:38.200
Like I'm gonna go swim the next two,

3490
02:23:38.200 --> 02:23:40.880
three hours at this pace,

3491
02:23:40.880 --> 02:23:43.490
I would usually suggest at least 500.

3492
02:23:43.490 --> 02:23:45.710
I personally do a thousand.

3493
02:23:45.710 --> 02:23:48.470
And then that pace gives me a good idea

3494
02:23:48.470 --> 02:23:52.913
of what my true aerobic zone 2 swimming pace would be.

3495
02:23:54.135 --> 02:23:55.240
So for us let's say,

3496
02:23:55.240 --> 02:23:57.200
just so that you get a number around it,

3497
02:23:57.200 --> 02:24:01.440
let's say it's 120 right now, 121.

3498
02:24:01.440 --> 02:24:03.320
Literally you just go all day pace.

3499
02:24:03.320 --> 02:24:06.010
If I had to swim 10,000 straight right now,

3500
02:24:06.010 --> 02:24:07.760
at what effort level would I start?

3501
02:24:07.760 --> 02:24:10.160
And that's what I wanna swim that thousand that,

3502
02:24:11.166 --> 02:24:14.150
well over time, we'll notice from that sensation.

3503
02:24:14.150 --> 02:24:15.630
What we usually know is heart rate

3504
02:24:15.630 --> 02:24:17.600
when we're outside biking and running,

3505
02:24:17.600 --> 02:24:19.130
that that time will come down.

3506
02:24:19.130 --> 02:24:22.237
Same effort level that it's going down to a 118

3507
02:24:22.237 --> 02:24:23.800
and then 117.

3508
02:24:23.800 --> 02:24:28.800
So we keep one sensation, the same output level,

3509
02:24:28.870 --> 02:24:33.393
feel RPE, and the time improves as we're getting fitter,

3510
02:24:34.250 --> 02:24:36.150
but we want that at the end of the workout.

3511
02:24:36.150 --> 02:24:38.220
Otherwise our RPE and our sensation

3512
02:24:38.220 --> 02:24:40.114
is gonna be a little bit off.

3513
02:24:40.114 --> 02:24:42.180
So that's why it's key to sort of burn off

3514
02:24:42.180 --> 02:24:46.340
the anaerobic juices and especially muscle glycogen 2.

3515
02:24:46.340 --> 02:24:48.410
And then with those tanks empty,

3516
02:24:48.410 --> 02:24:49.890
you get a better sense

3517
02:24:49.890 --> 02:24:54.890
and RPE of what you are truly going at aerobic pace at.

3518
02:24:55.077 --> 02:24:58.280
One of the techniques that you have deployed

3519
02:24:58.280 --> 02:25:01.070
with me over the years, that I think is really effective,

3520
02:25:01.070 --> 02:25:05.870
is making sure that your key discipline

3521
02:25:05.870 --> 02:25:08.300
is being trained under fatigue, right?

3522
02:25:08.300 --> 02:25:11.280
So in Ultraman, you never want to go out

3523
02:25:11.280 --> 02:25:12.500
and run on fresh legs

3524
02:25:12.500 --> 02:25:15.310
because that's not gonna be the experience at the race.

3525
02:25:15.310 --> 02:25:17.840
You always want your runs to be on the heels

3526
02:25:17.840 --> 02:25:22.110
of a very difficult cycling workout or swim workout.

3527
02:25:22.110 --> 02:25:24.240
So that every time you're running you're tired,

3528
02:25:24.240 --> 02:25:25.660
in this case because this,

3529
02:25:25.660 --> 02:25:28.580
it's just one discipline, but it is so long.

3530
02:25:28.580 --> 02:25:32.140
I suspect at some point during this training cycle,

3531
02:25:32.140 --> 02:25:33.530
you're gonna throw some stuff at me,

3532
02:25:33.530 --> 02:25:37.880
like maybe a difficult ride right before that swim.

3533
02:25:37.880 --> 02:25:39.130
So how do you think about,

3534
02:25:39.130 --> 02:25:40.690
or what do you have in store for me

3535
02:25:40.690 --> 02:25:43.673
in terms of stressing me in that way.

3536
02:25:44.580 --> 02:25:47.310
I love negative split swimming.

3537
02:25:47.310 --> 02:25:50.942
Where you have to start the first half of whatever it is

3538
02:25:50.942 --> 02:25:54.160
and make the second half faster.

3539
02:25:54.160 --> 02:25:55.940
So that you A, you learn your pacing,

3540
02:25:55.940 --> 02:25:57.830
but B, you really have to dig deep

3541
02:25:57.830 --> 02:26:00.980
in order to make that second half faster.

3542
02:26:00.980 --> 02:26:03.090
So you're coming into that second half

3543
02:26:03.090 --> 02:26:07.377
of those 800s of those 1000s of let's say, 4100s,

3544
02:26:08.220 --> 02:26:11.210
each 10, you're progressing the interval,

3545
02:26:11.210 --> 02:26:14.720
things like that where you were coming into the last 10

3546
02:26:14.720 --> 02:26:17.510
with a pretty good load on the arms

3547
02:26:17.510 --> 02:26:20.760
and the body and the whole system.

3548
02:26:20.760 --> 02:26:22.330
So similarly like that,

3549
02:26:22.330 --> 02:26:24.220
now of course we can do with cycling,

3550
02:26:24.220 --> 02:26:25.860
but it's a different type of fatigue.

3551
02:26:25.860 --> 02:26:28.096
It's actually in my opinion, a little bit better running,

3552
02:26:28.096 --> 02:26:32.950
but again we don't need that for what you're planning to do.

3553
02:26:32.950 --> 02:26:36.240
I think what you're gonna find is long swim workouts,

3554
02:26:36.240 --> 02:26:39.310
and then having a money set as I like to call it,

3555
02:26:39.310 --> 02:26:40.510
at the back end.

3556
02:26:40.510 --> 02:26:44.980
So let's say you just swam a 6,000 or 7,000 yard workout,

3557
02:26:44.980 --> 02:26:46.757
and then we do a money set and you're like,

3558
02:26:46.757 --> 02:26:47.590
"Oh really?"

3559
02:26:47.590 --> 02:26:49.870
Putting the main set at the very end of the workout.

3560
02:26:49.870 --> 02:26:51.623
Exactly, exactly.

3561
02:26:51.623 --> 02:26:53.740
And again that builds confidence

3562
02:26:53.740 --> 02:26:56.060
that knowing at two hours in,

3563
02:26:56.060 --> 02:26:59.493
I can still do X, Y, Z. That feels good.

3564
02:27:00.330 --> 02:27:02.610
One of the things that I always experience,

3565
02:27:02.610 --> 02:27:05.020
and I've shared this in the training logs with you,

3566
02:27:05.020 --> 02:27:08.690
when I start to get back in the water with some consistency,

3567
02:27:08.690 --> 02:27:11.300
is that I begin with one gear.

3568
02:27:11.300 --> 02:27:12.830
Like I have an aerobic base

3569
02:27:12.830 --> 02:27:14.980
so I can get in and swim back and forth fine,

3570
02:27:14.980 --> 02:27:16.690
but the minute I have to ramp it up

3571
02:27:16.690 --> 02:27:17.913
and do something hard,

3572
02:27:19.660 --> 02:27:21.930
My arms won't do what my brain is telling them to do

3573
02:27:21.930 --> 02:27:23.610
because I don't have the strength.

3574
02:27:23.610 --> 02:27:26.300
And to the extent that I can ramp it up a little bit,

3575
02:27:26.300 --> 02:27:28.960
I can't sustain it for any significant period of time.

3576
02:27:28.960 --> 02:27:30.960
Like I just completely fall apart.

3577
02:27:30.960 --> 02:27:33.390
So as we build that aerobic base

3578
02:27:33.390 --> 02:27:35.900
and start throwing down some tempo sets

3579
02:27:35.900 --> 02:27:38.110
and descending sets, etc.

3580
02:27:38.110 --> 02:27:40.260
That starts to slowly come together,

3581
02:27:40.260 --> 02:27:42.190
and then I start paying attention

3582
02:27:42.190 --> 02:27:44.470
to what we were talking about earlier.

3583
02:27:44.470 --> 02:27:46.180
Like how many gears do I have?

3584
02:27:46.180 --> 02:27:48.240
Can I go to two gears and then three gears

3585
02:27:48.240 --> 02:27:51.010
and four gears, and how much control do I have?

3586
02:27:51.010 --> 02:27:53.880
Like if I'm doing a set of descending 100s,

3587
02:27:53.880 --> 02:27:56.060
can I really lock in and make sure

3588
02:27:56.060 --> 02:27:59.562
that I'm inching down in time with each one

3589
02:27:59.562 --> 02:28:03.090
in a consistent way and the better adapted

3590
02:28:03.090 --> 02:28:05.440
I am to doing that, the more fit I am

3591
02:28:05.440 --> 02:28:10.020
and the more quickly my body will reset the baseline,

3592
02:28:10.020 --> 02:28:12.060
particularly on short rest,

3593
02:28:12.060 --> 02:28:13.440
that's a really good indicator

3594
02:28:13.440 --> 02:28:16.443
that the fitness is starting to come online.

3595
02:28:17.302 --> 02:28:19.940
As well as what you're also gonna notice

3596
02:28:19.940 --> 02:28:23.330
is you are your understanding, your feel of pace

3597
02:28:23.330 --> 02:28:26.070
is gonna be critical in open water.

3598
02:28:26.070 --> 02:28:30.660
So you don't start too hot or too slow on event day.

3599
02:28:30.660 --> 02:28:33.040
And you wanna be able to know

3600
02:28:33.040 --> 02:28:35.240
what that pace is no matter what,

3601
02:28:35.240 --> 02:28:38.490
even if you're hungry, even if you're fatigued,

3602
02:28:38.490 --> 02:28:40.460
even if you're whatever it is,

3603
02:28:40.460 --> 02:28:43.760
whatever the burden on you is

3604
02:28:43.760 --> 02:28:45.830
that you still can click into

3605
02:28:45.830 --> 02:28:48.400
whatever your open water swim pace is.

3606
02:28:48.400 --> 02:28:52.131
Or at least you can feel what 110 is like,

3607
02:28:52.131 --> 02:28:55.530
what 115 is like, and what 120 is like and so forth.

3608
02:28:55.530 --> 02:28:56.950
I was talking to somebody today,

3609
02:28:56.950 --> 02:28:59.130
he's doing a last man standing event.

3610
02:28:59.130 --> 02:29:02.140
It's gonna be critical that you know your pace

3611
02:29:02.140 --> 02:29:05.360
and the same thing for open water, there's no clock.

3612
02:29:05.360 --> 02:29:07.887
So you wanna be able to just know,

3613
02:29:07.887 --> 02:29:09.380
"Okay, I'm swimming pretty well.

3614
02:29:09.380 --> 02:29:12.537
I can feel my pace is going very well."

3615
02:29:13.880 --> 02:29:17.680
One of the things that I have to get comfortable with

3616
02:29:17.680 --> 02:29:20.110
is knowing that I'm gonna show up at this race,

3617
02:29:20.110 --> 02:29:22.963
not as fully prepared as I would like to.

3618
02:29:23.942 --> 02:29:25.660
And that kicks in a lot of ego stuff.

3619
02:29:25.660 --> 02:29:26.850
Like I don't want to tow the line,

3620
02:29:26.850 --> 02:29:29.880
unless I know that I've put in 110%

3621
02:29:29.880 --> 02:29:31.410
and earned the right to be there

3622
02:29:31.410 --> 02:29:33.940
and have taken it seriously, etc.

3623
02:29:33.940 --> 02:29:36.680
And that's just not the reality of my busy life.

3624
02:29:36.680 --> 02:29:41.680
So can I show up at 65% or 70%,

3625
02:29:43.440 --> 02:29:44.900
depending upon how busy I get?

3626
02:29:44.900 --> 02:29:49.460
You're just like every one of my other athletes.

3627
02:29:49.460 --> 02:29:52.041
I can't, and like still have fun

3628
02:29:52.041 --> 02:29:55.270
and let go of all of that other bullshit

3629
02:29:55.270 --> 02:29:56.877
because who the fuck cares?

3630
02:29:56.877 --> 02:30:01.877
Exactly. Well, your current 110%, that's the key.

3631
02:30:01.990 --> 02:30:03.980
That's key that unlocks this all.

3632
02:30:03.980 --> 02:30:07.330
You cannot compare yourself to 25-year-old Rich,

3633
02:30:07.330 --> 02:30:10.600
35-year-old Rich, 45-year-old Rich.

3634
02:30:10.600 --> 02:30:13.250
It's your current 110%.

3635
02:30:13.250 --> 02:30:18.030
If you feel you did what you could going into this event,

3636
02:30:18.030 --> 02:30:20.572
it takes so much of a burden off.

3637
02:30:20.572 --> 02:30:23.470
You can't be somebody different, you can only be you.

3638
02:30:23.470 --> 02:30:27.800
And your ability to do what you currently can,

3639
02:30:27.800 --> 02:30:29.500
that's going to be critical.

3640
02:30:29.500 --> 02:30:31.120
That's showing up with intention

3641
02:30:31.120 --> 02:30:33.810
because you know this is all I can do.

3642
02:30:33.810 --> 02:30:37.540
I'm not, futzing around watching Netflix all day.

3643
02:30:37.540 --> 02:30:40.140
I've got a busy life, but when I do show up,

3644
02:30:40.140 --> 02:30:43.320
I give it my best and come event day,

3645
02:30:43.320 --> 02:30:46.110
you will have that to fall back upon.

3646
02:30:46.110 --> 02:30:48.357
Is there always wishful thinking of,

3647
02:30:48.357 --> 02:30:50.930
"Well, back in the day, I could have done this?"

3648
02:30:50.930 --> 02:30:52.170
Of course there is.

3649
02:30:52.170 --> 02:30:55.950
But you can't be that person again, that's the past.

3650
02:30:55.950 --> 02:30:58.790
And you're gonna not enjoy your day

3651
02:30:58.790 --> 02:31:01.580
and this experience nearly as much,

3652
02:31:01.580 --> 02:31:04.730
if you're stuck in the past version of yourself.

3653
02:31:04.730 --> 02:31:07.990
I will say that it's a lot less time consuming

3654
02:31:07.990 --> 02:31:10.570
to just swim than to do all the other nonsense.

3655
02:31:10.570 --> 02:31:13.680
That takes up so much time, you know?

3656
02:31:13.680 --> 02:31:16.570
It's like, wow an hour and a half and I'm done for the day

3657
02:31:16.570 --> 02:31:19.155
and it's just, yeah, it's on the way to work or whatever.

3658
02:31:19.155 --> 02:31:22.274
It's like, that's not so bad.

3659
02:31:22.274 --> 02:31:26.450
Yeah, the main thing is for me over the next week or so,

3660
02:31:26.450 --> 02:31:29.230
or two weeks is that you really understand what we're doing,

3661
02:31:29.230 --> 02:31:30.670
why we're doing it

3662
02:31:30.670 --> 02:31:33.530
and get a good sense of where we're progressing to.

3663
02:31:33.530 --> 02:31:36.260
And like we talked about, we have some longer workouts,

3664
02:31:36.260 --> 02:31:37.670
we have some shorter stuff.

3665
02:31:37.670 --> 02:31:39.720
If you have extra time,

3666
02:31:39.720 --> 02:31:41.670
I'm gonna give you an extra workout or two

3667
02:31:41.670 --> 02:31:43.100
and put it into training peaks

3668
02:31:43.100 --> 02:31:44.930
so that you can choose from the library

3669
02:31:44.930 --> 02:31:46.640
and draw down from that.

3670
02:31:46.640 --> 02:31:50.140
And that we sort of navigate through these next two,

3671
02:31:50.140 --> 02:31:51.880
three weeks with some consistency

3672
02:31:51.880 --> 02:31:54.041
that you'll feel good like,

3673
02:31:54.041 --> 02:31:55.450
"I'm progressing, I'm not just treading water,

3674
02:31:55.450 --> 02:31:56.460
I'm progressing."

3675
02:31:56.460 --> 02:31:59.730
And you're gonna find that just being in the pool frequently

3676
02:31:59.730 --> 02:32:02.330
is gonna automatically do that for you.

3677
02:32:02.330 --> 02:32:05.513
Yeah, so much of it is the consistency.

3678
02:32:05.513 --> 02:32:07.544
But final thing I wanted to ask you is,

3679
02:32:07.544 --> 02:32:10.990
what are my blind spots right now?

3680
02:32:10.990 --> 02:32:12.260
When you're looking at my logs

3681
02:32:12.260 --> 02:32:14.000
or you're thinking about getting me ready

3682
02:32:14.000 --> 02:32:15.990
and you knowing me as well as you know me,

3683
02:32:15.990 --> 02:32:20.075
like when you have a shake your head moment,

3684
02:32:20.075 --> 02:32:22.522
what is it that you want to tell me?

3685
02:32:22.522 --> 02:32:23.890
(both laughing)

3686
02:32:23.890 --> 02:32:25.837
Well, one, it's training where you are

3687
02:32:25.837 --> 02:32:27.770
and not where you want be.

3688
02:32:27.770 --> 02:32:29.710
That's the key and that's when you jump ahead

3689
02:32:29.710 --> 02:32:32.770
and do the 5,000 yards because it feels good.

3690
02:32:32.770 --> 02:32:34.870
And of course in our mind,

3691
02:32:34.870 --> 02:32:37.660
we go, "Okay, that's a quarter of the race, that's great."

3692
02:32:37.660 --> 02:32:41.170
I can already in March do a quarter of my day,

3693
02:32:41.170 --> 02:32:43.840
but again we're building along a plan.

3694
02:32:43.840 --> 02:32:47.360
There's a path, there's a clarity to where we're heading.

3695
02:32:47.360 --> 02:32:50.890
And so we gotta trust the process, number one.

3696
02:32:50.890 --> 02:32:52.655
And then secondly,

3697
02:32:52.655 --> 02:32:55.740
you've brought both the things up already.

3698
02:32:55.740 --> 02:32:57.900
The other one is be good to yourself.

3699
02:32:57.900 --> 02:33:02.800
This is gonna be fun. This is where you exhale.

3700
02:33:02.800 --> 02:33:04.700
This is where we don't wanna judge ourselves

3701
02:33:04.700 --> 02:33:06.780
and compare ourselves to past versions,

3702
02:33:06.780 --> 02:33:08.490
but just really embrace.

3703
02:33:08.490 --> 02:33:11.930
Look at this, I get to swim outside in California

3704
02:33:11.930 --> 02:33:15.610
on my way to work, feel great, have a lot of energy,

3705
02:33:15.610 --> 02:33:17.910
fill my cup before I go to work

3706
02:33:17.910 --> 02:33:20.150
in just good physical activity.

3707
02:33:20.150 --> 02:33:21.540
It's something I love to do.

3708
02:33:21.540 --> 02:33:24.180
We always get outta the water feeling awesome

3709
02:33:24.180 --> 02:33:26.500
and like invigorated and that was pretty good.

3710
02:33:26.500 --> 02:33:28.600
Yeah, our arms might be a little tired,

3711
02:33:28.600 --> 02:33:32.254
but the whole cleansing aspect of swimming is so powerful.

3712
02:33:32.254 --> 02:33:35.165
And yeah, go with those two things,

3713
02:33:35.165 --> 02:33:37.660
it's gonna be fine.

3714
02:33:37.660 --> 02:33:40.120
You're gonna have a blast doing this event.

3715
02:33:40.120 --> 02:33:43.260
I think you're really gonna enjoy open water swimming.

3716
02:33:43.260 --> 02:33:48.210
I'm excited for you and you will be ready.

3717
02:33:48.210 --> 02:33:49.330
It's like what I told you

3718
02:33:49.330 --> 02:33:52.200
when you just did wildflower triathlon

3719
02:33:52.200 --> 02:33:53.870
way back many years ago.

3720
02:33:53.870 --> 02:33:54.703
And you're like,

3721
02:33:54.703 --> 02:33:56.040
"Dude, I'm thinking about Ultraman."

3722
02:33:56.040 --> 02:33:56.873
And I was like,

3723
02:33:56.873 --> 02:33:57.920
"I'll get you ready."

3724
02:33:57.920 --> 02:33:59.800
This isn't the question of if,

3725
02:33:59.800 --> 02:34:00.950
just a question of how.

3726
02:34:02.230 --> 02:34:05.370
Well, if nothing else just having this conversation

3727
02:34:05.370 --> 02:34:07.660
with you and sharing it publicly,

3728
02:34:07.660 --> 02:34:09.790
which makes me feel very vulnerable,

3729
02:34:09.790 --> 02:34:13.610
makes it so much less likely

3730
02:34:13.610 --> 02:34:16.770
that I'm gonna like cop out and then not show up.

3731
02:34:16.770 --> 02:34:19.030
So if it serves no other master,

3732
02:34:19.030 --> 02:34:22.390
other than to hold me accountable to show up,

3733
02:34:22.390 --> 02:34:25.923
then I know that's part of your dastardly plan,

3734
02:34:27.099 --> 02:34:28.220
but it's effective.

3735
02:34:28.220 --> 02:34:30.450
Yeah. It's training weeks, not workouts.

3736
02:34:30.450 --> 02:34:33.090
Keep that in mind, training weeks, not workouts.

3737
02:34:33.090 --> 02:34:35.150
So you just keep stacking the workouts.

3738
02:34:35.150 --> 02:34:38.223
You'll stack the training weeks and it'll all come together.

3739
02:34:39.580 --> 02:34:41.690
Excellent man. Well, I'll do my best.

3740
02:34:41.690 --> 02:34:45.450
And I'll check in with you in another two weeks publicly

3741
02:34:45.450 --> 02:34:48.600
And you can take my address

3742
02:34:48.600 --> 02:34:50.030
and tell me what I'm doing wrong

3743
02:34:50.030 --> 02:34:51.340
and tell me what I'm doing right.

3744
02:34:51.340 --> 02:34:53.440
And we'll just go from there.

3745
02:34:53.440 --> 02:34:55.540
Remember, be intentional with the whole thing.

3746
02:34:55.540 --> 02:34:58.070
And also as you're going through it,

3747
02:34:58.070 --> 02:35:01.030
something I always like to tell athletes is,

3748
02:35:01.030 --> 02:35:04.090
what does this look like when it's going well?

3749
02:35:04.090 --> 02:35:07.020
So as you look ahead of your week of training

3750
02:35:07.020 --> 02:35:08.860
and go what does this week look like

3751
02:35:08.860 --> 02:35:10.140
if it went really well?

3752
02:35:10.140 --> 02:35:12.030
On Friday, how will wear on Sunday,

3753
02:35:12.030 --> 02:35:12.937
how will I look back and go,

3754
02:35:12.937 --> 02:35:15.177
"You know what? That was a pretty good training week."

3755
02:35:16.743 --> 02:35:17.960
It takes us out of the intervals

3756
02:35:17.960 --> 02:35:19.620
and the pace and more bigger picture.

3757
02:35:19.620 --> 02:35:20.573
I had a good week.

3758
02:35:21.980 --> 02:35:23.440
Yeah, one of the things that you've done

3759
02:35:23.440 --> 02:35:25.740
is kind of create a bunch of workouts.

3760
02:35:25.740 --> 02:35:26.720
And then I say to you what,

